# Old WordPress addresses (worldschoolingjourneys.com before the move): what happens to them.
# Imported by the worldschoolingjourneys.com site block (see server/Caddyfile.site). Copy to the VPS:
#   scp server\old-site-redirects.caddy melike@178.105.202.222:~/   then on the VPS: sudo cp ~/old-site-redirects.caddy /etc/caddy/
#
# The old site's pages live at /travel/... on the old WordPress (cPanel host 107.155.113.78), which stays online.
#   - An old page with a real equivalent on the new site (the same trip, a cruise/trip listing, a page with the same name
#     like /travel/about/ -> /about) redirects there (301).
#   - Every other old page (testimonials, press, blog, past trips, categories, forms, Coming Soon ideas...) keeps showing
#     from the old WordPress at its usual /travel/... address. So do the doc and excursion pages and their forms.
#   - /travel itself -> the new home page.
# Made 2026-10-14 from the old site's sitemap; changed 2026-10-16 to redirect only real equivalents.

# The address without the /travel in front (the list below works for both /travel/x/ and /x/).
map {path} {old_path} {
        ~^(?:/travel)?(/.*)$                       ${1}
}

# Old pages with a real equivalent on the new site. Cruise targets use the booking code: the cruise page switches the
# address to its current name.
map {old_path} {old_site_target} {
        /trips/                                                                    /cruises                                               # no certain match
        /trips                                                                     /cruises
        /trips/december-panama-canal-cruise/                                       /cruises/PC-03DEC2026-LOS-FOR                          # booking code on old page
        /trips/december-panama-canal-cruise                                        /cruises/PC-03DEC2026-LOS-FOR
